      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To compute the determinant of a 2x2 matrix \\(\\begin{vmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{vmatrix}\\), we use the formula \\(ad - bc\\).\n\nFor the given matrix \\(\\begin{vmatrix} 7 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 \\end{vmatrix}\\), we identify the elements as follows:\n- \\(a = 7\\)\n- \\(b = 3\\)\n- \\(c = -1\\)\n- \\(d = 2\\)\n\nNow, we apply the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Determinant} = ad - bc = (7 \\cdot 2) - (3 \\cdot -1)\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate the product of \\(a\\) and \\(d\\):\n\n\\[\n7 \\cdot 2 = 14\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate the product of \\(b\\) and \\(c\\):\n\n\\[\n3 \\cdot -1 = -3\n\\]\n\nNow, subtract the second product from the first:\n\n\\[\n14 - (-3) = 14 + 3 = 17\n\\]\n\nThus, the determinant of the given matrix is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{17}\n\\]",
