    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To compute the determinant of a \\(2 \\times 2\\) matrix \\(\\begin{vmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{vmatrix}\\), we use the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Determinant} = ad - bc\n\\]\n\nGiven the matrix:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{vmatrix} 7 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 \\end{vmatrix}\n\\]\n\nwe can identify the elements as follows:\n- \\(a = 7\\)\n- \\(b = 3\\)\n- \\(c = -1\\)\n- \\(d = 2\\)\n\nNow, substitute these values into the determinant formula:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Determinant} = (7 \\cdot 2) - (3 \\cdot -1)\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\(7 \\cdot 2\\):\n\n\\[\n7 \\cdot 2 = 14\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(3 \\cdot -1\\):\n\n\\[\n3 \\cdot -1 = -3\n\\]\n\nNow, subtract the second result from the first:\n\n\\[\n14 - (-3) = 14 + 3 = 17\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the determinant of the matrix is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{17}\n\\]",
