      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the determinant of the given 2x2 matrix \\(\\begin{vmatrix} 7 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2 \\end{vmatrix}\\), we use the formula for the determinant of a 2x2 matrix \\(\\begin{vmatrix} a & b \\\\ c & d \\end{vmatrix}\\), which is \\(ad - bc\\).\n\nHere, \\(a = 7\\), \\(b = 3\\), \\(c = -1\\), and \\(d = 2\\). Substituting these values into the formula, we get:\n\\[\n\\text{Determinant} = (7 \\cdot 2) - (3 \\cdot -1)\n\\]\nFirst, we calculate the products:\n\\[\n7 \\cdot 2 = 14\n\\]\n\\[\n3 \\cdot -1 = -3\n\\]\nNow, we substitute these products back into the formula:\n\\[\n\\text{Determinant} = 14 - (-3)\n\\]\nSubtracting a negative is the same as adding the positive, so we have:\n\\[\n\\text{Determinant} = 14 + 3 = 17\n\\]\nTherefore, the determinant of the matrix is \\(\\boxed{17}\\).",
